From d924cd92156db0ccb37f3403d6376a4af939a102 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Jose M. Caballero Guerrero"
 <80172778+Caballero-git@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 14:08:31 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 21/30] arm64: dts: rockchip: P25T: panel timing node, active
 line 3 px earlier

Describe the panel timing in the device tree (read by the jadard
driver, previous patch) so it can be tuned on the tablet with fdtput.

With the stock display-timings (hfp 18, hsync 18, hbp 18) every panel
line showed 3 px late: the last pixels of a line appeared at the start
of the next one, cutting the top of the first console row in landscape
and showing it at the bottom; rows near the top of the frame flickered
on coloured backgrounds (tests/test_18.sh). Moving 3 px from the back
porch to the front porch (hfp 21, hbp 15; same line length, 60 Hz)
fixes it - found with tests/tune_panel.sh, confirmed 2026-10-02.

Tried first and rejected: continuous DSI clock lane (stock dsi,flags
0xa03 minus LPM) - panel black; negative hsync/vsync (stock) - colour
channels rotated by one byte and a ~20 px wrap. So no polarity
properties here: the default (positive) is correct on this board.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-teclast-p25t.dts | 26 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 26 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-teclast-p25t.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-teclast-p25t.dts
index 2223790c9..b6b603ead 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-teclast-p25t.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-teclast-p25t.dts
@@ -416,6 +416,32 @@ panel@0 {
 		reset-gpios = <&gpio3 RK_PC3 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
 		vdd-supply = <&vcc_lcd>;
 		vccio-supply = <&vcc_1v8_dummy>;
+		width-mm = <135>;
+		height-mm = <216>;
+
+		/*
+		 * Patch 0025: the timing as a DT node, read by the jadard driver
+		 * (patch 0024) instead of its built-in mode; it can be tuned on
+		 * the tablet with fdtput (tests/tune_panel.sh). Stock values
+		 * except the horizontal porches: with the stock hfp 18 / hbp 18
+		 * each line showed 3 px late (the line end wrapped to the next
+		 * line start) and rows near the frame top flickered
+		 * (tests/test_18.sh); hfp 21 / hbp 15 sends the data 3 px
+		 * earlier, same line length (confirmed 2026-10-02). No polarity
+		 * properties: the default (positive) is right here, the stock
+		 * negative ones rotate the colour channels.
+		 */
+		panel-timing {
+			clock-frequency = <67000000>;
+			hactive = <800>;
+			vactive = <1280>;
+			hfront-porch = <21>;
+			hsync-len = <18>;
+			hback-porch = <15>;
+			vfront-porch = <12>;
+			vsync-len = <4>;
+			vback-porch = <8>;
+		};
 
 		port {
 			mipi_in_panel: endpoint {
